      "note": "THE APPRENTICE CONVERGED. Live against qwen3-coder:30b on hex, 2026-08-18T06:23:52Z: a scratch repo whose check.py demands the literal token SENTINEL-4417 inside add.__doc__ — a requirement deliberately ABSENT from the 255-char brief and absent from calc.py's pre-drive bytes. Attempt 1 wrote `return a + b` and failed. aider ran the test itself, the failure text set reflected_message, and the apprentice's second reply opens `I need to add a docstring to the add function that contains the exact token \"SENTINEL-4417\"`. That token existed in exactly one place the model could have read it: the assertion message, reachable only through aider's own in-process run. The parent's run_test then returned 0. This is the first drive in the device's life where the apprentice was WRONG, was TOLD, and FIXED IT — the whole point of the ticket, and it is a live measurement, not a fixture. Five criteria answered by their instruments, all pass; five hypotheses dispositioned, four confirmed and ONE KILLED. The kill is criterion 5's: the charter hypothesis claimed this device's charter was the only artifact describing how the driver constructs the Coder, and the corpus grep found a second one still standing in class-space after the charter moved — test_driver.py's own MISMATCH_REPLY docstring, saying auto_test is OFF by bound. Words-kept-meanings-replaced, caught at n=1 where the prior instance cost eight sites, and fixed inside this voyage. TWO MEASUREMENTS THE VOYAGE OWES FORWARD. (1) THE HOST TIMEOUT IS SHORTER THAN A COLD LOAD: the first live fire died `HostUnmetered ... response carried ['created_at','done','message','model']`, and the cause is not the shape it names. hex needs ~131s to bring qwen3-coder:30b up at the fence's num_ctx 81920 (measured: total_duration 131.5s of which prompt_eval 0.5s and eval 0.3s — the rest is KV allocation), while host.DEFAULT_TIMEOUT is 120.0s. Warm, the same two asks take 4-6s each. ollama omits zero-valued counters, so a request th